From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:05:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] build: Target the Apple M1 instruction set in the ARM64X
 cross file.

Every macOS 27 Mac has an M1 or newer, so build both halves of the PE
code for ARMv8.5 with FP16FML, AES and SHA3: atomics become LSE
instructions instead of LL/SC loops. Tuning stays generic; Apple tuning
crashes llvm-mingw's SEH unwind emitter. The link arguments are
unchanged. The translator is built with Apple clang, so translated
shaders don't change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 build-arm64ec.txt | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build-arm64ec.txt b/build-arm64ec.txt
index e9ac3b4..af9e93c 100644
--- a/build-arm64ec.txt
+++ b/build-arm64ec.txt
@@ -9,8 +9,8 @@ windres = 'arm64ec-w64-mingw32-windres'
 needs_exe_wrapper = true
 
 [built-in options]
-c_args = ['-marm64x']
-cpp_args = ['-marm64x']
+c_args = ['-marm64x', '-march=armv8.5-a+fp16fml+aes+sha3']
+cpp_args = ['-marm64x', '-march=armv8.5-a+fp16fml+aes+sha3']
 c_link_args = ['-marm64x']
 cpp_link_args = ['-marm64x']
 
-- 
